    Specification(standard_code='2', spec_code='b', standard_title='Philosophical Base of Programs', spec_text='Demonstrate alignment with the mission of the units in which the program is housed (e.g., department, college, university, etc.).', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='2', spec_code='c', standard_title='Philosophical Base of Programs', spec_text='Provide a brief description of the major knowledge base and theories from which the curriculum draws to support the conceptual framework (e.g. counseling theories, biopsychosocial model, systems theory, change theory, etc.).', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='2', spec_code='d', standard_title='Philosophical Base of Programs', spec_text='Describe the multidisciplinary, interdisciplinary, or transdisciplinary approach to knowledge, theories, and skills included in the curriculum.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='2', spec_code='e', standard_title='Philosophical Base of Programs', spec_text='Provide a matrix mapping the curriculum Standards (11-18) and Specifications to required courses. The information provided on the matrix must clearly align with the information presented in the self-study narrative and the syllabi. NOTE: The Matrix must include required courses for all students that contribute to compliance with the Curriculum Standards and their Specifications. If a program has specific concentrations, identify the specific core courses in the concentration that comply with a Standard and its Specifications.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='3', spec_code='a', standard_title='Community Assessment', spec_text='If the program is less than five years old, provide documentation that supported the initial development of the human services program (such as a community needs assessment).', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='3', spec_code='b', standard_title='Community Assessment', spec_text='An Advisory Committee shall be established to provide feedback on local, state, and national trends and needs, as well as policy changes, and to act as an advocate for the program. The committee should include individuals representing the human services field, such as: field experience agencies, employing agencies, citizen advocacy groups, alumni, current students, adjunct faculty, and other people related to the field of human services.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='3', spec_code='c', standard_title='Community Assessment', spec_text='Provide the following: 1. A detailed description of the membership of the Advisory Committee (e.g., names, agencies, roles, relationship to program, etc.), 2. Minutes of advisory committee meetings from the last two years 3. A narrative or table of how the committee interfaces with the program in relation to specific issues.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='3', spec_code='d', standard_title='Community Assessment', spec_text='Describe other mechanisms, if any, used to respond to changing needs in the human services field.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='4', spec_code='a', standard_title='Program Evaluation', spec_text='The program has clear, measurable student learning outcomes that align with the standards and an assessment plan that has been implemented. Provide the following: 1. Measurable student learning outcomes 2. Assessment plan (including timelines) 3. Examples of assessment tools (e.g., rubrics, exams, portfolios, surveys, capstone evaluations, etc.).', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='4', spec_code='b', standard_title='Program Evaluation', spec_text='The program must conduct a formal program evaluation at least every five years. The formal evaluation shall include student surveys, agency surveys, graduate follow-up surveys (directed to both graduates and their employers), active participation of the advisory committee, involvement of agencies where students are in field placements, course and faculty evaluations, and evaluative data mandated or conducted by the institution. Provide the following: 1. A history of program evaluations 2. A description of the methodology 3. A summative analysis of the most recent evaluation 4. A description of how and in what way the evaluation resulted in any change.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='4', spec_code='c', standard_title='Program Evaluation', spec_text='The program must provide reliable information on its performance (including student achievement data) to the public from the last two years. [NOTE: This Specification relates to accreditation standards or policies that require institutions or programs to provide timely, readily accessible, accurate, and consistent aggregate information to the public about institutional or programmatic performance and student achievement, as the institution or program determines such information. (Paragraph 12 (B)(1), 2019 CHEA Recognition Policy and Procedures)] Provide the following: 1. An active link to student achievement indicators on the Program’s website. 2. . Aggregate data as evidence of student achievement. Include as many of the following as available: enrollment trends, retention, student learning outcomes, graduation rates, grade point average, student satisfaction, agency feedback, graduate transfer rates, graduate school or employment data, and alum surveys', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='5', spec_code='a', standard_title='Policies and Procedures for Admitting, Retaining, and Dismissing Students', spec_text='Provide documentation of policies regarding the selection and admission of students.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='5', spec_code='b', standard_title='Policies and Procedures for Admitting, Retaining, and Dismissing Students', spec_text='Provide documentation of policies and procedures for referring students for personal and academic assistance. These policies must be consistent with the institution’s policies.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='5', spec_code='c', standard_title='Policies and Procedures for Admitting, Retaining, and Dismissing Students', spec_text='Provide documentation of written policies and procedures describing the due process for remediation, probation, dismissal, appeal, and grievance procedures affecting students.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='5', spec_code='d', standard_title='Policies and Procedures for Admitting, Retaining, and Dismissing Students', spec_text='Provide documentation of program policies and procedures for assessing and managing student attributes, characteristics, and behaviors (“fitness for the profession”) that are important for the success of human service professionals', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='6', spec_code='a', standard_title='Credentials of Human Service Faculty', spec_text='Include the curriculum vitae of full-time and part-time faculty who teach human services courses. The vitae must demonstrate that: 1. Faculty have education in various disciplines and experience in human services or related fields. 2. If students choose a field placement as one of their graduation requirements, the involvement of field placement staff should meet the same educational requirements as teaching faculty. 3. Teaching faculty should have no less than the actual certificate or degree in which they teach. It is recommended that faculty have a doctoral degree.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='7', spec_code='a', standard_title='Personnel Roles, Responsibilities, and Evaluation', spec_text='Document that the program has ultimate responsibility for setting policies and determining the content, implementation, and evaluation of the curriculum.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='7', spec_code='b', standard_title='Personnel Roles, Responsibilities, and Evaluation', spec_text='Essential program roles include administration, curriculum development and review, instruction, field supervision, program planning, program evaluation, student advising, and student evaluation. 1. Provide a brief description of how these essential roles are fulfilled in the program. 2. Provide a table matching faculty and staff positions and names with these roles.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='7', spec_code='c', standard_title='Personnel Roles, Responsibilities, and Evaluation', spec_text='Describe the process for faculty and staff evaluation. Documentation may come from a variety of sources and may include, among others, student evaluations, administrative review, comments from field placement agencies, and peer review.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='7', spec_code='d', standard_title='Personnel Roles, Responsibilities, and Evaluation', spec_text='Describe how faculty and staff are provided opportunities for relevant professional development.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='8', spec_code='a', standard_title='Cultural Competence', spec_text='Demonstrate how the program 1. Includes intercultural fluency, and accessibility principles in program policies, procedures, and practices. 2. Includes intercultural fluency, accessibility principles training for faculty and staff', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='8', spec_code='b', standard_title='Cultural Competence', spec_text='Demonstrate how the curriculum integrates culturally inclusive, appropriate standards: 1. Includes but is not limited to student self-awareness of their own culture, biases, prejudice, and belief systems, and stereotyping. 2. Includes the development of awareness, knowledge, and skills of intercultural fluency, accessibility, and culture.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='9', spec_code='a', standard_title='Program Support', spec_text='Include budgetary information that demonstrates sufficient funding, faculty, and staff to provide an ongoing and stable program.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='9', spec_code='b', standard_title='Program Support', spec_text='Describe how program and field experience responsibilities are considered in calculating the teaching loads of faculty.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='9', spec_code='c', standard_title='Program Support', spec_text='Describe how the program has adequate professional support staff to meet the needs of students, faculty, and administration.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='9', spec_code='d', standard_title='Program Support', spec_text='Describe how there is adequate resource support (e.g., technology, library, computer labs, etc.) to meet the needs of students, faculty, and administration.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='10', spec_code='a', standard_title='Evaluation of Transfer Credits', spec_text='Describe formal policies and procedures, and informal practices for the transfer of credits', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='10', spec_code='b', standard_title='Evaluation of Transfer Credits', spec_text='Describe how students receive this information. Curriculum Standards - Master’s Degree A master’s degree program in Human Services requires scholarly and professional activities designed to advance the student substantially beyond the educational requirements of a baccalaureate degree program. The degree is structured to prepare students for professional practice through the creative application of knowledge, theory, and skills. The curriculum provides opportunity for a broad conceptual mastery of the field through an understanding of subject matter, bibliographical resources, theory, practice, and scholarly research. The curriculum aims to develop in students the capacity to interpret, analyze, synthesize, and communicate knowledge, as well as the skills necessary to practice and advance the profession effectively. The master’s degree in human services differs from a counseling degree in that graduates are prepared to contribute to positive change through a wide range of service and administrative roles within organizations, rather than delivering therapeutic services.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='11', spec_code='a', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Historical and current legislation affecting human services delivery.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='11', spec_code='b', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='How public and private attitudes influence legislation, and the interpretation of policies related to human services.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='11', spec_code='c', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Exposure to a spectrum of socio-political ideologies and how they influence human service delivery.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='11', spec_code='d', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Skills to analyze and interpret historical data for application in advocacy and social change. 2. Human Systems Context: The human services professional must understand the structure and dynamics of organizations, communities, and society as well as the nature of individuals and groups. This understanding is a prerequisite to the determination of appropriate responses to human needs.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='12', spec_code='a', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Overview of how administrators may work with groups such as boards of directors, community groups, public officials, or client/consumer advisory groups.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='12', spec_code='b', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='An introduction to the organizational structures of communities.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='12', spec_code='c', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='An understanding of the capacities, limitations, and resiliency of human systems.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='12', spec_code='d', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Emphasis on context and the role of intercultural fluency, including cultural group membership and individual identities in determining and meeting human needs.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='12', spec_code='e', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Processes to effect social change through advocacy work at all levels of society including community development, community and grassroots organizing, and local and global activism. 3. Human Services Delivery Systems Context: The demands for services, funding of educational programs, social justice, and advocacy have been closely related but not limited to aging, delinquency, crime, poverty, mental illness, physical illness, chemical dependency, and disabilities. The needs that arise provide the focus for the human services profession.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='13', spec_code='a', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='The range and characteristics of human services delivery systems and organizations.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='13', spec_code='b', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='The range of populations served, and needs addressed by human services.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='13', spec_code='c', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='The major models used to conceptualize and integrate prevention, maintenance, intervention, rehabilitation, and healthy functioning.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='13', spec_code='d', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Economic and social class systems, including systemic causes of poverty.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
