    Specification(standard_code='14', spec_code='d', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Knowledge and skills to compile, synthesize, and categorize information and present it orally and/or in writing to clients, colleagues, or other members of related services systems and to utilize the information for community education and public relations.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='14', spec_code='e', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Information literacy encompasses the skills necessary to effectively locate, evaluate, and utilize information from library databases, the World Wide Web, and other electronic resources.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='14', spec_code='f', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Familiarity with methods, statistics, quantitative and qualitative research, and the application of technology.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='14', spec_code='g', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Critical thinking for analysis, problem solving, synthesis, decision making, and predicting outcomes.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='14', spec_code='h', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Inclusion of a culminating capstone experience, e.g. research project, scholarly paper, or action research project. 5. Program Planning and Evaluation Context: A major component of the human services profession involves assessing the needs of clients and client groups, and planning programs and interventions to assist them in promoting optimal functioning, growth, and goal attainment. At regular intervals, the outcomes must be evaluated, and necessary adjustments made to the plan, both at an individual client and program level.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='15', spec_code='a', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Program planning and design.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='15', spec_code='b', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Program implementation.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='15', spec_code='c', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Program evaluation.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='15', spec_code='d', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Knowledge, theory, and skills to perform a community-needs assessment. 6. Administrative Leadership Context: A holistic approach to human services recognizes direct and indirect services as components of the same system. Administrative support (indirect service) is essential to the effective delivery of direct services to clients or client groups', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='16', spec_code='a', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Organizational management.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
