    Specification(standard_code='16', spec_code='e', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Fund development and fundraising (grants, special events, major gifts, etc.) and contract negotiation', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='16', spec_code='f', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Legal/regulatory issues and risk management, including issues related to nonprofit status.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='16', spec_code='g', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Supporting the professional development of staff.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='16', spec_code='h', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Recruiting and managing volunteers.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='16', spec_code='i', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Constituency building and other advocacy techniques such as lobbying, grassroots movements, and community development and organizing.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='16', spec_code='j', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Understanding the mission, vision, and ethical responsibilities of organizations and society as outlined by the Ethical Standards of the National Organization for Human Services (available at https://www.nationalhumanservices.org/ethical-standards-for-hs- professionals). 7. Legal and Ethical Practices Context: An understanding of laws, legal issues, and professional ethics as they relate to human services is necessary for informed practices and the protection of the rights of others.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='17', spec_code='a', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Respect for and maintaining the confidentiality of information.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='17', spec_code='b', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Recognition that individuals, service systems, and society change.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='17', spec_code='c', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Interprofessional approaches to problem solving.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='17', spec_code='d', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Respect for appropriate professional boundaries.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='17', spec_code='e', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Maintaining behavior that is congruent with the values and ethics of the profession as outlined by the Ethical Standards of the National Organization for Human Services (available at https://www.nationalhumanservices.org/ethical-standards-for-hs- professionals).', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='17', spec_code='f', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Clarification of values.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='17', spec_code='g', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Differentiation between ethical and legal standards. 8. Culminating Experiences Context: Culminating experiences are learning experiences in a human services delivery organization. It is a process of experiential learning that integrates the knowledge, theory, skills, and professional behaviors that are concurrently taught in the classroom. CSHSE requires master’s degree students to complete a learning experience that demonstrates competency in translating theory into practice, such as fieldwork experiences, a thesis, or an action research project. All options require a self-reflection process.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='18', spec_code='a', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Demonstrate that students are adequately exposed to human services agencies and clients (assigned visitation, observation, assisting staff, etc.)', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='18', spec_code='b', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Demonstrate criteria, policies, and procedures for determining when a student is required to complete a fieldwork experience. Fieldwork may be waived if the student has extensive experience, provided specific criteria, policies, and procedures are followed and documented. For those who qualify to have fieldwork waived, they must complete a capstone project, thesis, or an action research project.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='18', spec_code='c', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text="If a fieldwork experience is required, 1. Provide a copy of the current manual and guidelines that are given to students, advising them of field placement requirements. 2. Provide documentation of written agreements with field agencies that specify the student's role, activities, outcomes, supervision, and field instruction. 3. Provide syllabi for required seminars. Seminar hours are not included in field experience hours. 4. Provide evidence that a minimum of one academic credit is awarded for each three hours of weekly field experience. 5. Demonstrate that field experience is structured with clear learning outcomes and methods of evaluation.", program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='18', spec_code='d', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='If a fieldwork experience is required, 1. Demonstrate that the field supervisors have a minimum of a master’s degree or comparable years of professional experience. It is strongly recommended that field supervisors have no less than 10 years of professional experience if they do not hold a master’s degree. 2. Demonstrate that the program continually monitors the progress of each student and performs no less than one site visit to each field placement site per quarter or semester. The visit can be held as a direct site visit or with appropriate technology. The technology used should ensure that both the field placement supervisor and the student can be identified. 3. Demonstrate that there is a written plan of learning objectives, activities, and outcomes for each student that was conjointly developed and agreed to by the student, the program, and the agency supervisor. 4. the program shall provide a minimum of 100 clock hours of field experience in a human service setting. 5. The program shall provide a capstone experience, either a thesis, action research, or a program development/evaluation proposal, that demonstrates conceptual mastery of the professional practice. Demonstrate the rationale for the selected capstone experience option.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='18', spec_code='e', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='If fieldwork experience is waived, the program shall provide a capstone experience, either a thesis or action research, that demonstrates conceptual mastery of the professional practice. Provide the specific criteria and expectations for completing the selected capstone experience.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
    Specification(standard_code='18', spec_code='f', standard_title='Knowledge, Theory, Skills, and Values', spec_text='Demonstrate that a reflection on professional self (e.g., journaling, development of a portfolio, or project demonstrating competency) is included for the selected capstone experience: fieldwork, thesis, or action research.', program_level='masters', version="2025"),
